s related to the municipality of Cartagena in the Region of Murcia, Spain. It is part of the Regional Network of Museums of Murcia.","wpu":"Municipal Archaeological Museum of Cartagena","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3c/MuseoarqueologicoCartagena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Escombreras","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.559444,"lo":-0.969167,"d":4350,"ds":"Escombreras is an islet within a natural park at the mouth of the port of Cartagena, Spain in the Region of Murcia. A breakwater was built in 2011 for the expansion of the port has hooked around the north side of the island, but it does not connect to it. The steep islet covers 4 hectares (9.9 acres).","wpu":"Escombreras","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a8/Escombreras.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Cartagena (Spanish: [kaɾtaˈxena] ) is a city in the Region of Murcia in Spain. As of 2024, with a population of 219,235, it is the second most populated municipality in the Region of Murcia. The city lies in a natural harbour of the Mediterranean coastline of the southeast of the Iberian Peninsula.","wpu":"Cartagena, Spain","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ab/Cartagena_palacio_consistorial5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}